<title> GI Foreign Bodies: Management.</title>
<graphic href="eee0190-w001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Determine type of foreign body.</label>
<path target="cell-2">Coin</path>
<path target="cell-10">Food</path>
<path target="cell-11">Sharp object or battery</path>
<path target="cell-12">Magnet</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Determine location.</label>
<path target="cell-7">Esophagus</path>
<path target="cell-8">Stomach</path>
<path target="cell-9">Intestine</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>Remove immediately if symptoms, or observe for 24 h if asymptomatic.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Observe with serial radiographs. Remove if abdominal pain.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-9">
<label>Observe with serial radiographs. Remove if abdominal pain or signs of obstruction.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-10">
<label>If esophagus, remove immediately.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-11">
<label>Determine location.</label>
<path target="cell-13">Esophagus</path>
<path target="cell-14">Stomach</path>
<path target="cell-15">Intestine</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-12">
<label>All locations: If more than one magnet is ingested, immediate surgical consultation.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-13">
<label>Remove immediately.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-14">
<label>Observe with serial radiographs. Remove if abdominal pain.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-15">
<label>Observe with serial radiographs. Remove if abdominal pain or signs of obstruction.</label>
</cell>
